Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (AC5)
Why this approach: the plan's name test. Each gateway helper turns capture on (recording sink, real Budget, 32 MiB cap) when t.Name() starts with TestCapture_ForwardingUnchanged/, which reaches nested subtests and leaves 001's test bodies unchanged; subtests are named from the function itself, so the list can't drift from a typo.
Alternatives rejected: a registry keyed by *testing.T (misses nested subtests); editing 001's tests to pass a capture option (changes their bodies).
Trade-off / known limit: the listed 001 functions run twice per go test run (about 1s extra); a 001 test added later is only covered once someone adds it to the list. The anthropic wrapper's sink counts and releases rather than keeping exchanges. 001 AC11 is left out because it never reaches the proxy.
Verified by: TestCapture_ForwardingUnchanged in internal/core (18 functions) and internal/protocols/anthropic (9, including 001 AC9, AC10 and AC13, whose count_tokens, /v1/models, HEAD /api/hello and unknown-path exchanges are the parse-skipped ones) under -race; with the wrappers renamed, every subtest failed on "sink holds 0 exchanges" and was reverted; make verify.
